@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 64B ("בן זוג רשום", the registered spouse) and s 65 ("חישוב מאוחד", the
-- consolidated calculation). Row IL-08. Source lines 2439-2448.
--
-- GAPS.md item 3 of row IL-07: where no separate calculation under s 66 governs, the couple is
-- assessed under s 65, which row IL-02 names as an outcome and does not compute; and s 64B fixes who
-- the registered spouse is, which the capstone takes as an input.
--
-- s 64B is a set of powers and an election: the assessing officer MAY determine the registered
-- spouse, on a test of income two years back; the couple MAY elect the other spouse, on conditions;
-- the choice stands five years, subject to exceptions. Who is in fact the registered spouse is the
-- determination or election made, which a notice records: still an input. What is encoded here is
-- each condition the text puts on the power and on the election, so that a caller can check that a
-- recorded designation was open to be made.
--
-- s 65 says whose income the couple's income is: all of it is the registered spouse's, charged in his
-- name, together with four kinds of income of his child under 18. It computes no tax. The tax on that
-- income is s 121 (row IL-03); the credits in the registered spouse's computation are each section's
-- own (ss 34, 36, 36A in row IL-01; ss 35(b), 37, 38, 39 in this row). s 66 applies "על אף האמור
-- בסעיף 65" (row IL-02): where it gives a separate calculation, s 65 does not govern that income.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 64B — the registered spouse`

-- src:2439 | סעיף 64ב – בן זוג רשום [תיקון: תשנ״ב־6, תשנ״ו, תשנ״ו־5, תשס״ה־4, תשע״ד־3]
-- src:2440 | (א) פקיד השומה רשאי לקבוע, בהודעה לכל שני בני זוג, כי אחד מהם הוא בן זוג רשום לענין חוק זה, באשר הכנסתו החייבת בשנת המס שקדמה בשנתיים לשנת המס הנדונה לראשונה לענין זה היתה למעלה מ־50% מסך כל ההכנסה החייבת של שני בני הזוג.

GIVEN `which`  IS A `Which of the couple`
      `couple` IS A `A couple, for section 64B`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 64B — the taxable income two tax years before, of` `which` `in` `couple` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which`
    WHEN `the first spouse`  THEN `couple`'s `the first spouse's taxable income two tax years before it`
    WHEN `the second spouse` THEN `couple`'s `the second spouse's taxable income two tax years before it`

-- "למעלה מ־50%": more than half, strictly.
@ref ITO s 64B(a), line 2440
GIVEN `which`  IS A `Which of the couple`
      `couple` IS A `A couple, for section 64B`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `which` `is the registered spouse of` `couple` MEANS
    `s 64B — the taxable income two tax years before, of` `which` `in` `couple`
        GREATER THAN 50% TIMES (   `couple`'s `the first spouse's taxable income two tax years before it`
                              PLUS `couple`'s `the second spouse's taxable income two tax years before it`)

-- src:2442 | (ג) בני זוג שלא היתה לאף אחד מהם הכנסה חייבת בשנת המס האמורה בסעיף קטן (א), רשאי פקיד השומה לקבוע אחד מהם לבן זוג רשום, ולא יהיה בכך כדי לגרוע מזכותם לפעול לפי סעיף קטן (ב).
@ref ITO s 64B(c), line 2442
GIVEN `couple` IS A `A couple, for section 64B`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64B(c) — neither spouse had taxable income two tax years before, so the assessing officer may determine either, for` `couple` MEANS
        `couple`'s `the first spouse's taxable income two tax years before it` EQUALS 0
    AND `couple`'s `the second spouse's taxable income two tax years before it` EQUALS 0

-- Equal incomes: neither is above 50%, and (c) needs both at nil; the text gives the officer no power
-- to determine either (fork F32). Encoded as written: both rules answer FALSE.

-- src:2441 | (ב) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א) רשאים בני זוג ביחד להודיע בכתב לפקיד השומה, לפחות שלושה חדשים לפני תחילתה של שנת מס פלונית, כי הם בוחרים שבן הזוג האחר ייחשב כבן זוג רשום ובלבד שהכנסתו בשנת המס שקדמה לשנת המס שבה ניתנה ההודעה היא לפחות בגובה של 25% מהכנסת בן זוגו; לענין סעיף קטן זה וסעיף קטן (ד)(2), ”הכנסה בשנת המס“ – למעט הכנסה ממקור הכנסה משותף לפי סעיף 66(ד) שלא מתקיימות לגביה הוראות אותו סעיף.
-- "לפחות שלושה חדשים לפני תחילתה של שנת מס פלונית": on or before 1 October of the year before
-- (fork F31). The incomes are "income in the tax year" as the subsection defines it (without
-- common-source income that fails s 66(d)), which the caller supplies.
@ref ITO s 64B(b), line 2441
GIVEN e IS AN `An election of the registered spouse, for section 64B(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` e MEANS
        e's `made jointly and in writing by both spouses`
    AND e's `the day the notice was given` AT MOST YMD (e's `the first tax year it is to govern` MINUS 1) 10 1
    AND e's `that spouse's income in the tax year before the notice year`
            AT LEAST 25% TIMES e's `the other spouse's income in the tax year before the notice year`

-- src:2443 | (ד)(1) בכפוף לאמור בסעיף קטן (ב), קביעה או בחירה של בן זוג רשום תעמוד בתקפה לא פחות מחמש שנות מס זולת אם בני הזוג אינם עוד בני זוג, או על פי החלטת המנהל.
-- src:2444 | (2) על אף הוראות פסקה (1), היתה בשנת מס הכנסתו של בן הזוג הרשום לפי בחירה פחותה מ־25% מהכנסת בן זוגו באותה שנת המס, רשאי פקיד השומה לקבוע בן זוג רשום לאותה שנת מס.
-- "תעמוד בתקפה לא פחות מחמש שנות מס": the designation binds for the tax year it first governs and
-- the four after; after that it may be changed.
-- Version 0.2.0: this form answers the five-year term only. Its name lists the two exceptions, but
-- it takes no fact about either, nor about a later election "subject to (b)" (D271, D273). INPUT
-- CONVENTION: a caller of this form states that the couple are still spouses, that the Director has
-- not decided that the designation no longer stands, and that no later election under (b) is to
-- govern the year; one who does not know uses the form below, which takes those facts. The
-- independent tests call this form with two years (their D269 and D270 state none of the three).
@ref ITO s 64B(d)(1), line 2443
GIVEN `the first year`  IS A NUMBER
      `the year`        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64B(d)(1) — a determination or election first governing tax year` `the first year` `still stands, unless they cease to be spouses or the Director decides, in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` AT LEAST `the first year` AND `the year` AT MOST `the first year` PLUS 4

-- Version 0.2.0 (D271, D273). The exceptions, and "בכפוף לאמור בסעיף קטן (ב)":
--   "זולת אם בני הזוג אינם עוד בני זוג": once the couple are no longer spouses (s 1, src:112: married,
--     living together and running a joint household), the designation no longer stands;
--   "או על פי החלטת המנהל": nor once the Director has decided so;
--   "subject to (b)": the couple may elect under (b) "notwithstanding (a)", so a later election
--     displaces a determination of the assessing officer within its five years (the independent
--     pass's D272). Whether a later election displaces an earlier ELECTION within its five years the
--     text does not say: "subject to (b)" may reach every designation, or only the officer's, which
--     (b) itself overrides ("על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א)"). Declined (fork F36).
@ref ITO s 64B(d)(1), line 2443: whether an election under (b) displaces an earlier election within its five years
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 64B(d)(1) does not say whether a later election under subsection (b) displaces an earlier election within its five tax years` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 64B(d)(1) does not say whether a later election under subsection (b) displaces an earlier election within its five tax years"

@export Whether a determination or an election of the registered spouse still binds in a tax year under Income Tax Ordinance s 64B(d)(1): for five tax years, unless the couple have ceased to be spouses, the Director has decided otherwise, or a later election under s 64B(b) governs the year; declines where a later election would displace an earlier election
@ref ITO s 64B(d)(1), line 2443
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
          @desc the tax year asked about
      d          IS A `A designation of the registered spouse, for section 64B(d)(1)`
          @desc the designation: by the assessing officer under s 64B(a) or (c), or by the couple's election under (b); the first tax year it governs; whether the couple have since ceased to be spouses, the Director has decided it no longer stands, or a later election under (b) is to govern the year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64B(d)(1) — the designation still binds in tax year` `the year` `:` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT `s 64B(d)(1) — a determination or election first governing tax year` (d's `the first tax year it governs`) `still stands, unless they cease to be spouses or the Director decides, in tax year` `the year`
        THEN FALSE
        IF   d's `the couple have ceased to be spouses since it first governed`
        THEN FALSE
        IF   d's `the Director has decided that it no longer stands`
        THEN FALSE
        IF   d's `a later election under subsection (b) is to govern the tax year`
        THEN CONSIDER d's `made by`
             WHEN `determined by the assessing officer under subsection (a) or (c)` THEN FALSE
             WHEN `elected by the couple under subsection (b)`
                 THEN `section 64B(d)(1) does not say whether a later election under subsection (b) displaces an earlier election within its five tax years`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref ITO s 64B(d)(2), line 2444
GIVEN `the elected spouse's income` IS A NUMBER
      `the other spouse's income`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64B(d)(2) — the assessing officer may determine the registered spouse for the year, the elected spouse having income` `the elected spouse's income` `against` `the other spouse's income` MEANS
    `the elected spouse's income` LESS THAN 25% TIMES `the other spouse's income`

-- src:2445 | (ה) המנהל רשאי לקבוע בכללים דרכי קביעה ובחירה של בן זוג רשום.
-- A power to make rules; no rules are in the source bundle. Nothing to compute.

§ `Section 65 — the consolidated calculation`

-- src:2447 | סעיף 65 – חישוב מאוחד [תיקון: תשל״ח־5, תשמ״ח־3, תשנ״ב־6, תשס״ב־9, תשס״ה־9]
-- src:2448 | הכנסת בני זוג יראוה לענין פקודה זו כהכנסת בן הזוג הרשום והיא תחוייב על שמו; ולענין הכנסות מחברה שקופה כהגדרתה בסעיף 64א1 והכנסות מריבית, מדמי ניכיון או מהפרשי הצמדה (לענין סעיף זה – ריבית) וכן מהכנסה שהועברה מקרן להשקעות במקרקעין, כהגדרתה בסעיף 64א2, או מרווח הון, יראו את הכנסותיו כאמור של בן הזוג הרשום ככוללות גם הכנסות כאמור של ילדו שטרם מלאו לו בשנת המס 18 שנים, אלא אם כן הנכסים שמהם היתה ההכנסה מריבית, מקרן להשקעות במקרקעין או מרווח הון, התקבלו בירושה, או שמקורם בפיצויים או בכספי ביטוח שהתקבלו בשל פגיעת גוף.

-- The two item rules below say what s 65 does with one item where s 65 governs the couple's income
-- (spouses within s 1, no separate calculation under s 66); whether it governs is the couple's facts,
-- which the entry points below take.
-- A child's item is the registered spouse's where: the child is his (his own child: row IL-02's fork
-- F5 reads the same words of s 66(a)(3)); had not turned 18 in the tax year (aged 17 or less in the
-- year: IL-02's F15); and the item is of one of the four kinds; and, for interest, a REIT's income or
-- capital gain, the asset did not come by inheritance or from compensation or insurance money for
-- bodily injury. The exception does not name income from a transparent company, so it does not reach
-- it (fork F33).
@ref ITO s 65, line 2448
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of a household's income, for section 65`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — the item is a child's income that counts as the registered spouse's:` `the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`'s `whose`
    WHEN `a child's, of the registered spouse` `the age` THEN
            `the age` AT MOST 17
        AND CONSIDER `the item`'s `kind`
            WHEN `income from a transparent company as defined in section 64A1`            THEN TRUE
            WHEN `interest, discount or linkage differences`                                THEN NOT `excepted`
            WHEN `income passed on by a real estate investment trust as defined in section 64A2` THEN NOT `excepted`
            WHEN `capital gain`                                                             THEN NOT `excepted`
            WHEN `any other income`                                                         THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE `excepted` MEANS `the item`'s `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury`

@ref ITO s 65, line 2448
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of a household's income, for section 65`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` `the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`'s `whose`
    WHEN `the registered spouse's` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the other spouse's`      THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `s 65 — the item is a child's income that counts as the registered spouse's:` `the item`

-- Version 0.2.0 (D292, D293). "הכנסת בני זוג": s 65 is about spouses, which s 1 defines (src:112) as a
-- married person living with, and running a joint household with, the one he is married to; a married
-- couple living apart are not spouses, and each is assessed alone. And s 66 applies "על אף האמור
-- בסעיף 65": where a separate calculation under it governs some of the couple's income, s 65 does not
-- govern that income, and what it still charges is s 66's question (row IL-02). Version 0.1.0 took
-- neither fact and could decline neither case.
-- src:112 | ”בן זוג“ – אדם נשוי החי ומנהל משק בית משותף עם מי שהוא נשוי לו;
@ref ITO s 65, line 2448; s 1 "בן זוג", line 112
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 65 is about spouses, and these two are not spouses within section 1, so each is assessed on his own income` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 65 is about spouses, and these two are not spouses within section 1, so each is assessed on his own income"

@ref ITO s 66 (row IL-02), applying "notwithstanding s 65"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a separate calculation under section 66 governs some of the couple's income, notwithstanding section 65, and section 66 is not encoded in this row` MEANS
    REFUSE "a separate calculation under section 66 governs some of the couple's income, notwithstanding section 65, and section 66 is not encoded in this row"

@export The taxable income charged in the registered spouse's name under Income Tax Ordinance s 65 (the consolidated calculation of spouses), for a tax year from 2024; declines a couple who are not spouses within s 1 (living apart) and one for whom a separate calculation under s 66 governs some of the income
@ref ITO s 65, line 2448; s 1 "בן זוג", line 112
GIVEN c           IS A `A couple in a tax year, for section 65`
          @desc the tax year, from 2024; whether the two are married, living together and running a joint household (s 1 "spouse"); whether a separate calculation under s 66 governs some of their income
      `the items` IS A LIST OF `An item of a household's income, for section 65`
          @desc every item of the spouses' taxable income, and each item of the registered spouse's children's income, with its kind and, for a child, the child's age in the tax year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, for the couple` c `, from` `the items` MEANS
    `for tax year` (c's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (BRANCH
            IF   NOT c's `married, living together and running a joint household`
            THEN `section 65 is about spouses, and these two are not spouses within section 1, so each is assessed on his own income`
            IF   c's `a separate calculation under section 66 governs some of the couple's income`
            THEN `a separate calculation under section 66 governs some of the couple's income, notwithstanding section 65, and section 66 is not encoded in this row`
            OTHERWISE sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD IF `s 65 — the item is charged in the registered spouse's name:` i THEN i's `taxable amount` ELSE 0) `the items`))

-- Version 0.1.0's entry point, kept (row IL-07's capstone calls it). INPUT CONVENTION: a caller of this
-- form states that the two are spouses within s 1 (married, living together and running a joint
-- household) and that no separate calculation under s 66 governs any of their income; one who does not
-- know both uses the form above, which takes them as inputs and declines otherwise.
@ref ITO s 65, line 2448
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of a household's income, for section 65`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` `the tax year` `, from` `the items` MEANS
    `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, for the couple`
        (`A couple in a tax year, for section 65` WITH
            `tax year`                                                                     IS `the tax year`
            `married, living together and running a joint household`                      IS TRUE
            `a separate calculation under section 66 governs some of the couple's income` IS FALSE)
        `, from` `the items`
